    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (12 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp06Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `initials` field is a read-only derived attribute on the owner response, so I followed the exact pattern already used for `displayName`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto`), alongside `displayName`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes `initials` from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   e.g. `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec's trailing-dot, dot-separated, upper-cased form.\n\nSince `firstName` and `lastName` are `@NotEmpty` (validated on create), the first-character access is safe for any persisted owner, and the null-guard mirrors the existing `displayName` mapping.",
